I want to make my existing APB project fully responsive for BOTH desktop/laptop and mobile phones.

IMPORTANT:
- The application must work properly on laptops/desktops AND smartphones.
- Do NOT make it mobile-only.
- Do NOT damage or remove the existing desktop layout.
- Do NOT simply shrink the desktop UI on mobile.
- Create a proper responsive design where the layout adapts intelligently according to screen size.
- Preserve all existing functionality, backend logic, APIs, database logic, authentication, and business logic.
- First inspect the existing project before making changes.
- Reuse the existing UI components, CSS, design system, and frontend architecture wherever possible.
- Do not rewrite the entire application.

==================================================
MAIN REQUIREMENT
==================================================

APB must provide a good user experience on:

- Mobile phones
- Tablets
- Laptops
- Desktop monitors

The same application should automatically adapt to the available screen width.

Example:

Mobile:
320px - 480px

Tablet:
481px - 1024px

Laptop/Desktop:
1025px+

Do not hard-code these exact breakpoints if the existing project already has a responsive system. Use the project's existing conventions when appropriate.

==================================================
DESKTOP/LAPTOP
==================================================

The existing desktop experience should remain fully usable.

On laptop/desktop:

- use the available horizontal space
- show appropriate multi-column layouts
- use sidebar navigation where appropriate
- display tables normally where useful
- show multiple dashboard cards in a row
- display analytics charts at useful sizes
- keep forms appropriately sized
- avoid excessive empty space
- maintain the existing desktop design

Do NOT unnecessarily convert desktop layouts into mobile-style cards.

==================================================
MOBILE
==================================================

On smaller screens:

- stack columns vertically where necessary
- make navigation mobile-friendly
- use hamburger/collapsible navigation if appropriate
- resize dashboard cards
- make buttons touch-friendly
- make forms single-column
- convert wide tables into cards or responsive layouts when necessary
- resize charts
- make product cards fit the screen
- make cart usable with touch
- prevent horizontal page scrolling

The mobile layout should be a proper adaptation of the desktop design, not a completely different application.

==================================================
RESPONSIVE NAVIGATION
==================================================

Desktop:

Use the existing desktop navigation/sidebar if present.

Mobile:

Adapt the navigation to something suitable for a small screen, such as:

- hamburger menu
- collapsible sidebar
- bottom navigation

Do not show a large desktop sidebar that consumes most of the phone screen.

The navigation should automatically adapt based on screen size.

Preserve role-based navigation.

Customer navigation and Owner navigation must remain separate according to the existing authentication/role system.

