==================================================
RESPONSIVE TABLES
==================================================

For desktop, keep useful tables as tables.

For mobile, if a table becomes too wide:

Option 1:
Convert rows into cards.

Option 2:
Use a carefully designed responsive table.

Option 3:
Allow horizontal scrolling ONLY for genuinely tabular data where conversion would hurt usability.

Do not allow the entire webpage to horizontally scroll.

==================================================
IMAGES
==================================================

Images must be responsive.

Use:

max-width: 100%;

where appropriate.

Do not distort aspect ratios.

Product images should adapt to:

- phone
- tablet
- laptop
- desktop

Use lazy loading where appropriate.

==================================================
PERFORMANCE
==================================================

The application should remain reasonably fast on:

- low-end Android phones
- normal smartphones
- laptops
- desktop computers
- slower mobile networks

Avoid unnecessary:

- animations
- huge images
- duplicate API requests
- heavy dependencies
- unnecessary JavaScript

Do not sacrifice desktop performance while optimizing mobile.

==================================================
NO HORIZONTAL OVERFLOW
==================================================

This is mandatory.

At every screen size:

- no accidental horizontal page scrolling
- no overflowing buttons
- no overflowing images
- no overflowing cards
- no text going outside containers
- no charts extending beyond viewport
- no navigation overflow

Use responsive CSS instead of fixed widths wherever appropriate.

Avoid unnecessary fixed widths such as:

width: 1200px;

Prefer:

width: 100%;
max-width: ...;

when appropriate.

==================================================
RESPONSIVE BREAKPOINT STRATEGY
==================================================

Use a consistent responsive strategy.

Do not scatter dozens of random media queries throughout the project.

Prefer:

- flexible widths
- CSS Grid
- Flexbox
- max-width
- minmax()
- clamp()
- responsive typography
- existing project breakpoints

Use media queries only when layout behavior actually needs to change.

==================================================
TYPOGRAPHY
==================================================

Text should remain readable on all devices.

Desktop:
Comfortable larger layout.

Mobile:
Readable without zooming.

Avoid:

- extremely small text
- excessive text
- fixed font sizes that break layouts

Use responsive typography where appropriate.

==================================================
BUTTONS
==================================================

Desktop buttons should remain compact and professional.

Mobile buttons should have enough touch area.

Do not make all desktop buttons huge.

Adapt button sizing based on screen size and context.

Primary actions should remain visually clear.

